<surname>Breslow</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Frank</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosenfeld</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name><name><surname>Norris</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Christopherson</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Rock</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Gottlieb</surname><given-names>SO</given-names></name><name><surname>Raff</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Perler</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Catecholamine and cortisol responses to lower extremity revascularization: correlation with outcome variables. Perioperative Ischemia Randomized Anesthesia Trial Study Group</article-title><source>Crit Care Med</source><year>1995</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>1954</fpage><lpage>1961</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7497717</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00003246-199512000-00003</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kollef</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>Levy</surname><given-names>NT</given-names></name><name><surname>Ahrens</surname><given-names>TS</given-names></name><name><surname>Schaiff</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Prentice</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Sherman</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The use of continuous i.v. sedation is associated with prolongation of mechanical ventilation</article-title><source>Chest</source><year>1998</year><volume>114</volume><fpage>541</fpage><lpage>548</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9726743</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1378/chest.114.2.541</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sha